Z||000005||WKDFIRO||04-25-2001||01:26 AM||||My 85 GT did that sporadicly and I noticed that it did that when it got hot (stop/go traffic, no ram air at all) and I have the manny tranny. One night I was taking the onramp, one of those down hill sweeping right turns to get onto the freeway and I was going pretty darn quick, the engine popped, sputtered and died. <P>Lets say it all together...Drop throttle oversteer!<P>Spun out and after coming within a yard of making a light pole my best friend I started it up again, righted myself and went home. Days later it finally died and wouldn't start no matter how much I tried and found that my coil had finally sparked its last. <P>Don't know if thats what you are experiencing but thats what it reminded me of. <P>Good luck to you!||||reg||12
Z||000006||Ed||04-25-2001||01:33 AM||||I'd check the fuel pump.  My Dodge Caravan did just the same thing.  Ran for a few minutes and then quit.  Is the pump loud? ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Johnson's85SE||04-25-2001||02:29 PM||||Hey,<BR> I had the same prob. What worked for me was changing the ignition module. After about five minutes, the engine compartment would heat up, and the module would disconnect. It wouldn't start until it cooled down.  Worked for me. <BR>Cheers!<P>------------------<BR>If it isn't broke, it's not my car.||||reg||1
Z||000008||kornholio||04-25-2001||05:43 PM||||I had the same problem you described.  I changed the TPS and it has been fine ever since.||||reg||1
Z||000009||DJRice||04-25-2001||07:23 PM||||If your oil pressure has been jumping around alot, then I pity you because we just went thru this on my brother's fiero.  His was dying because the pressure would drop and the oil psi switch would kill the fuel pump. <BR>Turns out he had a bad main bearing.....<P>But check the other stuff first...<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
